WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.660
- I got to say, we had your husband on

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:03.160
the show a few weeks ago

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:04.450
and first of all, I hope he had fun,

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:06.800
but also when you entered this screen,

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:08.270
like I've seen you in
movies, but I was like,

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:11.550
oh man, no in real life you
really are that attractive.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:14.923
And I was like, way to go,
DeVon, way to go DeVon.

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:18.340
You did well, sir.

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:19.760
I was like, geez,

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.170
you entered the screen and I was like,

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:22.590
is that what we we're
supposed to look like?

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:23.660
I don't understand.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:26.330
Anyway, you are, you are not
only so beautiful though,

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:27.163
you're so talented.

00:00:27.163 --> 00:00:29.240
I love the films that you're
in and I love your spirit

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:31.650
and I love DeVon, he was
so awesome on the show.

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:32.770
Did he have a good time?

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:33.603
- Thank you.

00:00:33.603 --> 00:00:35.160
Yes, he definitely had a good time.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.330
He had a great experience,

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:39.150
so I was so excited when I
found that I get to come too.

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:41.210
- I know at one point
I want you both here.

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:44.280
I want it 'cause I think
that dynamic would be funny,

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:45.280
but he talked about

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:48.360
how your relationship
got better in quarantine

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:51.790
and well, that is well
the opposite for my life

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:53.540
and maybe a lot of other people.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:56.860
So do you, do you feel the
same that it did get better?

00:00:56.860 --> 00:00:58.560
- Oh yeah, I do.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:00:59.393
- Wow.

00:00:59.393 --> 00:01:00.980
- It's weird because you
know, because of our jobs

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:03.620
we're often like ships
passing in the night

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:05.530
and I'll be gone for
you know, three months,

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:07.280
four months, seven months at a time,

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:09.810
he'll visit when he can, he'll
be gone for months at a time.

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:12.829
So for us, it was a
chance to just sit down,

00:01:12.829 --> 00:01:14.320
take a breather,

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:15.400
take each other in,

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.480
enjoy each other.

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:18.530
I started cooking more,

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:19.670
he started baking more.

00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:21.550
So we started cooking and baking together

00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:23.850
and listening to music and

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.160
we decided to get marriage counseling

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:28.950
just in the spirit of
like, let's be proactive.

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:30.550
Let's go look underneath the hood

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:31.960
and see if there's anything that maybe

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:32.900
hasn't been dealt with

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:35.270
or that we can work
through it, whatever it is

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:37.300
and we did it for like
probably five or six months

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:38.576
and it was amazing.

00:01:38.576 --> 00:01:41.170
Just the things that you discover that,

00:01:41.170 --> 00:01:43.560
you know just the trauma, past
traumas that you both have

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:46.656
and there's always an
opportunity to just be proactive

00:01:46.656 --> 00:01:49.710
in the marriage and say,
let's not just do something

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:52.180
if something happens,
but let's go do the work

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:54.350
and make it as, as you
know, as good as we can.

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:56.640
So it was a, it's pretty amazing,

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:58.400
it's definitely a transformative and

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:00.060
yeah.
- I think being

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:02.553
proactive about it, that's amazing.

